{
 "result": "maze.py is a padded-grid BFS. It reads stdin, splits rows, and pads a bytes buffer with a one-cell sentinel border so neighbour checks need no bounds tests. Rows are translated to 0/1 bytes in C, and the same buffer doubles as the visited set. It exits as soon as E is reached. It handles missing S or E and S==E. It matches all three public samples (2008, -1, 78). The adopted variant scored 3.488 against the 2.324 baseline, a +52% gain, and the assay is registered. I'm stopping here because the body is verified and already well above baseline, and further gains are likely small.",
